From f5e0a509121f3019962465827425b5c4aa8dda7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:01:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Network] Projector control: the test of the
 connection can be cancelled and is waited for a bounded time

The test runs on the thread of the control, the only one that talks to
the projector. Where that thread was waiting for a lens that moves (a
JVC answers a lens memory once the lens has stopped, up to a minute),
the settings waited for the test under the busy dialog without a way
to cancel it, up to a minute or more.

The settings now wait with a progress dialog that says why it may take
long and has Cancel, and for TestWaitMs() at most (the longest talk the
thread can be in when the test is asked, and the test's own, with their
gaps: 106 s with the timeouts of the protocols). A test that is not
waited for any more is taken back where the thread has not begun it,
or stopped where it runs (its talk stops at once: CSession's stop); a
test not answered in time says so ("did not answer within N seconds,
it may still be moving its lens"); a cancelled one says nothing. Each
test has a number, so that the answer of one that was given up is never
shown for the next. New strings #62770 and #62771, Estuary #54770 and
#54771, in English and Spanish.
